offset196. Preserve the 1496/1504/1520 publication extents and\nprocess-purpose8 envelope. Bind the declaration in the sealed initial record,\nrequire it on subsequent observations and reject every predecessor, zero and\nunknown edition before producing output. Rename every actual decoder caller,\nincluding the preinit literal closure, and refresh exact fixture fingerprints.\n\nDocument the producer promise: every born row, including dirty/unprojected\nrows, stays retained; exposed matching actions are irrevocably pending before\nrequest publication and cannot race unpublished abandonment. Exact action birth\ncannot be replaced until authenticated assigned-peer local closure. Local\nsubscriber closure never retires publisher-owned rows, and producer death or\nunknown cleanup does not certify physical return. This compatibility cut does\nnot yet construct a Source subscription or issue operation/action authority.\n\nExercise current syntax plus predecessor, edition, byte-order and unchanged\noutput refusals. Retain prior native causal timeout and launched lifecycle\nfailures as unresolved observations; no decoder or component result qualifies\nactivation, Original, publisher membership, ACK or ActionReturn.\n\nComplete the lifetime component's real constructor-RCU prerequisite before its\nforeign-process identity control forks. A child otherwise can restart RCU while\ninheriting the thread-registry mutex held by the vanished constructor helper.\nDrain actual RCU callbacks, then inspect the real registry under that mutex:\nexactly one retained RCU_RESTART helper, its coordinator, no overflow and no\nin-flight starts. Expose the actual starts counter in process-private inventory\nonly. Keep the helper record alive, every process-refusal assertion and all\nexisting build/test ceilings. No sleep, synthetic readiness or fork grant is\nsubstituted. Refresh exact extractor fingerprints after the native header edit.\n\nThe fixture starts no other QEMU threads in this scenari