later\nphysical cleanup cannot revive CALLING. Close semantic action before v4 payload,\nQOM/CPU, Source Main and descriptor return. Final module evidence precedes exact\ncanonical consumption; save consumption before independently refusing an\nincomplete healthy return. Legacy member editions remain semantic-unavailable.\n\nComponent controls exercise literal custody and writer bodies with real C\npayload journals, QOM retention and writable atomic mapping. Standing/assigned\ninstallation and local semantic boundary inputs are explicitly modeled; these\ncontrols do not qualify the installed Rust semantic path or launched lifecycle.\nRetain every original scenario, resource ceiling and refusal. Independently\nrebuilt publisher and literal evidence defects must fail their causal assertions.\nAdd five explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later files and retain all existing file licenses.\nKeep prior failed causal attempts and mandatory launched lifecycle refusal\nvisible; no operation/activation or peer-return qualification follows from\ncompilation or modeled component success.\n\n\nInclude the newly referenced actual Core Main/action predicates and their real\ninactive journal declarations in the owning Source/Native extractor closure.\nNo fixture may replace those predicates with successful authority providers.\nPreserve the first incomplete-closure link failure as a failed build attempt.\n\nRetain selected initial CPU callbacks under the actual stopped construction\nOriginal. Defer enqueue until each actual Source allocation receipt exists,\nretain its canonical QOM participant and registration group, and complete the\nreal CPU FIFO callback/barrier before construction Post. Authenticate distinct\ncallback entry, return and final physical consumption; pre-enqueue refusal\ncloses only the actual unentered child. Check actual roster generation after\nQOM unref before advancing its iterator. No FIFO marker invents callback return.\n\nGuard selected realized capability, manifest, bind, seal and register-list SDK\nfactories with the actual class-0 child and exact Core/Native callback. Preserve\nindependent first/post failures. Their missing bounded native constructor payer\nstill refuses before factory allocation with ENOKEY; unselected paths keep their\nexisting behavior. Generic VCPU_INIT remains factual and inactive; no new\nworkspace, operation, activation, ACK or physical peer-return permission exists.\n\nCharge the actual Core initial-dispatch static extent and enlarged actual CPU\nallocation owner through their existing paid layouts. Extract the real storage\nand getter for component sizing, retaining exact source and dependency guards.\nAdd two explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later includes. Literal clock and SDK-history tests\nexercise independent total/progress/clock and signed-history omission controls.\nThe assertion-only actual initial callback hooks remain unexecuted pending the\ngenuine installed-module launch harness; compilation and pure predicate tests\ncannot qualify that route. Preserve original ceilings, all previous failed\nattempts and mandatory launched Source/Root lifecycle refusal.\n\nReplace the hardware manifest and binding GArrays with the actual bounded\nsix-row/six-binding typed declaration. Preserve ordinary architecture branches,\nordering and binding behavior; refuse sticky overflow before publication.\nCharge the entire declaration once through its genuine installation floor,\nincluding its inactive lease and terminal journals, for the image lifetime.\n\nRetain the private paired hardware constructor lease under the actual initial\nCPU child, QOM allocation receipts, fixed account and construction Original.\nKeep actual Native issuing/holder predicates and post-ATEXIT process/thread\nscope distinct from installation or callback facts. Terminal return requires\nreal registry retirement and worker, material, action, Main, Ready, Park and\ninitial-CPU closure, plus no registered handlers, staged VMState or pending events.\nConsume logical lease dependencies only after unpublication; static image\nbacking remains charged. Selected public SDK and internal lazy builders remain\nprebirth-refused. These inactive seams do not qualify an accepted constructor,\nexecuted callback, operation, activation or physical peer return.\n\nRefuse selected register and interrupt lazy factories before CPU lookup or\ncached-row reuse, retaining unselected preconditions and behavior. Extract the\nactual typed catalogue declaration/getter and enlarged Core dispatch journal\nfor component sizing; retain exact source/dependency fingerprints. Run literal\nstorage/branch, selected refusal and physical-debt controls with independent\nomission mutations, and document actual installed-runner/factory prerequisites.\nAdd two explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later focused tests and preserve every existing\nfile license, assertion and resource limit. Initial callback and lease assertion\nhooks remain unexecuted; retain all prior failed attempts and the mandatory\nlaunched Source/Root lifecycle refusal.\n\nReplace the interrupt manifest, bindings and target arrays with the actual\nbounded typed 13-row, 13-binding and 4096-target catalogue. Preserve ordinary\narchitecture templates, ordering and realized-device evidence requirements;\nrefuse sticky row/target overflow before publication. Charge the exact image\nstorage once in the real fixed Native floor, without paying device strings,\nregistrations, handlers or future constructors by implication.\n\nKeep selected SDK and internal prebirth refusals unchanged. Exercise actual\nregister_family, builder, binding and sealing bodies with explicit CPU and\nrealized-capability inputs; independently rebuild missing-evidence, selected\nrefusal and target-overflow defects. Preserve the earlier register/interrupt\nrefusal controls under the actual typed layout. These facts issue no Source\npayer, accepted lease, entered callback, operation or activation authority.\n\nExtract the actual typed declaration and getter, guard every new source input,\nand run the new GPL-2.0-or-later focused test from the existing native driver.\nRetain its actual GLib link dependency from configured QEMU provider metadata.\nPreserve every earlier assertion, resource ceiling, failed attempt and mandatory\nlaunched Source/Root lifecycle refusal; initial callback and lease hooks remain\nunexecuted.\n\nCount the actual realized AArch64 register registry without constructing a\nsorted key workspace. Share the existing eligibility predicate with the\nunchanged sorted-key path; preserve explicit exception, EL and SVE rules and\nsaturate an unrepresentable count rather than wrapping. Geometry preflight is\na storage fact, not a Source payer, accepted lease, live callback or operation.\n\nCompare literal count and sorted keys against the independently frozen prior\neligibility rule across feature/exception variants and the over-limit registry.\nRebuild allocating-count and eligibility-change controls to their intended\nassertions. Integrate the GPL-2.0-or-later component into the actual native\ndriver with its real configured GLib dependency and guard exact source inputs.\nPreserve every original ceiling/refusal, prior failed attempt, unexecuted\ninitial hook and mandatory launched Source/Root lifecycle refusal. Descriptor\nworkspace, runtime/read and lifetime funding remain separate and unavailable.\n\nAdd architecture-owned factual register geometry, complete sorted key views\nand allocation-free descriptor writers for realized ARM and x86 cohorts.\nUse caller-retained name and four independent mask spans; check actual current\ngeometry, eligibility, ordering, capacities, overflow and disjoint spans before\npublishing each descriptor. Preserve allocating wrappers' ownership and prior\nfeature/exception/SVE names and mask semantics. These process-private CPUClass\nhooks issue no Source payer, manifest constructor, callback or operational use.\n\nExercise literal producer/helper bo